{
  "_readme": "Human-vote leaderboard signal (arena.ai, formerly LMArena/Chatbot Arena) for scripts/derive-signals.mjs's `families` calibration in assets/decide.mjs. Arena's leaderboard tables render client-side via JS — curl gets nav/footer only (verified by diffing curl output against a headless-browser render of the same URL), so this is NOT a live-fetched Collect input like usage.openrouter or this same signals pipeline's OpenRouter task-spend data. It is a DATED, MANUAL snapshot: fetched once via a headless browser (Claude_Browser, read-only) on 2026-09-07 against a page self-dated 'Sep 2, 2026', with the raw captures kept alongside the research batch that built it. `rank` is this model's position within the mapped-to-catalog cut for that task/category (1st mapped = rank 1, etc.) — NOT its raw position on Arena's own (much longer, mostly-unmapped) leaderboard; effort-level variants of the same base model (e.g. claude-opus-5-high / claude-opus-5-max) were de-duplicated to their best-ranked variant before this cut was taken. `category` names the actual Arena leaderboard or column used as each task's proxy — several tasks have no dedicated Arena category and use the closest available one (documented per task below and in eval/signals.md, which is the primary methodology doc this file was distilled from). Refresh procedure: scripts/refresh.md's 'Arena preferred boards' section — replace this file's `tasks` block and bump `as_of`; there is no automated refresh for this source. UPDATE 2026-09-07 (brain v2 step 2): the /leaderboard/vision, /leaderboard/document, /leaderboard/agent, and /leaderboard/search pages turned out to be a DIFFERENT case — arena.ai now serves these as dedicated per-category routes with the full leaderboard table rendered server-side directly into the HTML response (confirmed by diffing a plain `curl` fetch against the rendered DOM: identical rows), so those four were captured with a plain read-only GET, no headless browser needed. The Overview (/leaderboard) and Text-Arena (/leaderboard/text) pages, and the /leaderboard/webdev route (which doesn't exist — 404), remain client-rendered / absent as described above; check both ways on any future recapture rather than assuming one method covers every board.",
